THE FILES IN THIS DIRECTORY record the console reply layouts of the GSSquared
emulator's debugger, one reply kind per file, for Casso's GSSquared output
format to be compared against line by line. This note covers every file in
this directory and nothing outside it.

Work:      GSSquared, an Apple II and IIgs emulator
Author:    Jawaid Bazyar and contributors
Source:    https://github.com/jawaidbazyar2/gssquared
Read at:   commit 4a14e989754fa03ee8bde6bdb009ab62eff62ef9, 2026-09-18

HOW THEY WERE MADE. These are NOT captured from a running GSSquared. Building
it needs SDL3 and its other dependencies, which this machine does not have, so
each file was written by hand from the format strings in GSSquared's
src/debugger/Monitor.cpp (examine, dump, breakpoint and watch lists and their
"set" lines, save, slookup, sclear) and src/debugger/trace.cpp with
line_buffer.hpp (the column layout of `list`), applied to the values of the
program in ../Scripts/stop.txt and the data the formatter tests build. No
GSSquared source code is copied here or into Casso; only the layout of the
text it prints is reproduced, as a specification to test against.

Where Casso's reply is known to differ from what GSSquared would print for the
same command, the fixture records GSSquared's layout for the values Casso
produces, and the difference is recorded in the spec's research note R-027:

- `list` prints thirty instructions in GSSquared and twenty in Casso; the
  fixture has the two instructions the test builds.
- GSSquared pads its disassembly lines to a fixed width with trailing spaces;
  the fixtures, like Casso, carry no trailing spaces.
- GSSquared watches a range as one entry; Casso watches each address, so
  `watch 6.7` lists two single-address entries, as recorded here.

Tests MUST treat these files as read-only: a mismatch is a finding about
Casso, unless the file is shown to differ from GSSquared's own output.
